# Locales generated into the image.
#
# A skeleton tree, not an extra tree: skeleton trees are copied in before the
# package manager runs, so glibc's own locale-gen hook sees this file when it
# fires during installation. An extra tree is copied afterwards, too late for
# the hook, and generating the locale later would mean executing inside the
# image — which is what mkosi-chroot does and what nixpkgs' mkosi wrapper
# breaks.
#
# C.UTF-8 is built into glibc and needs no entry here.
en_US.UTF-8 UTF-8
